      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a pretty thin test and almost useless.  \n\n`pdc_power_mgmt_request_source_voltage()` also triggers a new power request which can renegotiate the contract with the charger.\n\nVerifying the contract gets renegotiated is the side effect you should be testing.\n\nI recommend this test flow:\n* Configure the partner\u0027s source PDOs to include a 5V, 15V, and 20V\n* Set max voltage to 5V.\n* configure sink, connect partner\n* Verify 5V PDO selected using `emul_pdc_get_rdo()`.\n* Set max voltage to 15V\n* Verify 15V PDO selected using `emul_pdc_get_rdo()`.\n\nYou also need a test that connects a DRP sink (PDC is the source), and verify that the PDC swapped to sink.",
